up04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_verification_fail_message\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_verification_fail_message\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_verification_fail_message\tExplain a completion failure. Label evidence-search exhaustion as insufficient evidence and append the verdict's remediation.\tPASS\t56\t15\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#C:_verification_fail_message:before:from rebar._commands import close_autoresume:1\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#C:_verification_fail_message:before:from rebar._commands import close_autoresume:1\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#C:_verification_fail_message:before:from rebar._commands import close_autoresume:1\t# Include attempt, cached PASS, and unmet counts only when the verifier # resumed.\tPASS\t48\t12\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#C:_verification_fail_message:before:message += (:1\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#C:_verification_fail_message:before:message += (:1\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#C:_verification_fail_message:before:message += (:1\t# Show applicable disposition classes for deliberately unfinished work.\tPASS\t54\t8\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_administrative_disposition\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_administrative_disposition\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_administrative_disposition\tReturn a deterministic disposition sign signal when a reason or usable replacement qualifies. Otherwise keep normal verification or return an unsigned disposition result.\tPASS\t51\t23\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_gate_skip_expectation\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_gate_skip_expectation\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_gate_skip_expectation\tRecord gate_off when disabled or force_bypassed when an enabled gate is forced. Resolve gate state first. Unreadable config raises instead of producing a skip.\tPASS\t113\t24\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_completion_precheck\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_completion_precheck\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py#D:_completion_precheck\tReturn the pre-close verdict and durable completion expectation. Use a signed completion PASS, a deterministic disposition, or an explicit reason why certification is absent. Fail closed on verifier failure or error. Import the optional LLM only when needed.\tPASS\t202\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:<module>\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:<module>\tCLI facade for ticket compaction and store-wide sweeps. The locked fold lives in compact_txn, full-log fsck rebuild in compact_rebuild, and shared derivations in compact_plan. This module re-exports their established names and reports sweep results.\tPASS\t169\t34\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_foldable_event_count\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_foldable_event_count\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_foldable_event_count\tCount events the locked fold can actually absorb under the horizon. Use the shared candidate listing and foldability rule. Exclude unknown event types, bridge metadata, retired files, and prior snapshots. An unreadable candidate counts only when the horizon is off.\tPASS\t252\t40\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_scan_snapshot_state\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_scan_snapshot_state\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_scan_snapshot_state\tReturn sorted ticket IDs needing a first snapshot or a recurrence fold, plus the remaining count. Backfill selects snapshotless tickets with any foldable event. Recurrence selects counts above threshold. Scan active tickets by default. include_archived restores migration coverage.\tPASS\t290\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_best_effort_push\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_best_effort_push\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_best_effort_push\tPush pending commits even when a sweep folded nothing. Skip for dry-run or no-commit. Preserve OptionalDependencyError from a misconfigured S3 remote instead of hiding it.\tPASS\t217\t25\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_snapshot_names\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_snapshot_names\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_snapshot_names\tReturn snapshot filenames, or empty on read error.\tPASS\t12\t8\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_should_yield\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_should_yield\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_should_yield\tCheck between tickets whether a foreground writer needs the lock. Leave remaining optional folds for a later sweep.\tPASS\t95\t18\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_one_ticket\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_one_ticket\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_one_ticket\tFold one ticket and return '.', '-', or 'E'. Count work only when a new snapshot appears because a successful return may also mean no fold. Commit each fold under its lock, except when the operator requested no-commit. Pushes remain batched.\tPASS\t151\t39\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_position_map\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_position_map\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact.py#D:_sweep_position_map\tBuild one position-keyed introducing-commit map before the sweep locks. The authorship ledger reads positions, so a path-keyed map would miss. Return None when building fails or yields nothing, allowing per-ticket fallback. An empty dict would trigger per-event history walks in the lock.\tPASS\t286\t42\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_plan.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_plan.py#D:<module>\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_plan.py#D:<module>\tShared compaction planner for normal fold, fsck rebuild, and recovery. Own candidate listing, snapshot envelope, retired-file restore, and commit derivations. Each engine keeps its own failure policy.\tPASS\t218\t27\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py#D:<module>\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py#D:<module>\tRebuild a snapshot from the full ordered event log for fsck repair. Share snapshot derivations with normal compaction. The rebuild tolerates per-file retire failures and resumes through its backup sentinel rather than the normal fold's rollback journal. Its counter stays beside the rebuild function and is re-exported by compact.\tPASS\t179\t49\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py#D:<module>\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py#D:<module>\tRecover interrupted folds through an intent journal outside the worktree. Before mutation, record snapshot and sources. Under the write lock, revert uncommitted snapshots, discard journals for committed or replaced snapshots, and leave retained inconsistent states for fsck repair.\tPASS\t283\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py#D:_revert_partial_fold\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py#D:_revert_partial_fold\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py#D:_revert_partial_fold\tRestore retired sources and unstage the ticket directory. Remove an uncommitted snapshot only after every source is restored. If restoration fails, retain the snapshot for fsck repair to avoid losing the folded event.\tPASS\t125\t33\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py#D:<module>\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py#D:<module>\tOperation-linked compaction trigger for environments without cron or CI. After close releases the store lock, make bounded eligibility checks and start a detached sweep worker. Use shared process and stamped-lock helpers. The waited-on close does not hold the lock through a fold.\tPASS\t295\t42\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py#D:run_sweep\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py#D:run_sweep\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py#D:run_sweep\tRun the same store-wide sweep as the scheduled workflow under its advisory worker lock. Let compact_all_cli stamp only a sweep that ran. A stand-aside leaves the clock unchanged so later closes retry.\tPASS\t130\t32\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:<module>\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:<module>\tLocked transaction for folding a ticket into one snapshot. Own horizon partitioning, placement, retire, and rollback. compact_plan shares derivations with fsck rebuild and recovery. The fold uses fsck's orphan predicate so it cannot absorb an orphaned event.\tPASS\t181\t37\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_build_authorship_ledger\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_build_authorship_ledger\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_build_authorship_ledger\tRecord signed folded events for later identity verification. Store content hash, signature, verifying key, position, and introducing commit, using null for failed best-effort lookups. Omit unsigned events. Use a supplied position-keyed commit map without git log, or build one per ticket. Misses fall back to per-event resolution.\tPASS\t372\t47\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_exclude_snapshot_orphans\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_exclude_snapshot_orphans\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_exclude_snapshot_orphans\tLeave active events predating the latest snapshot out of the fold when that snapshot never cited them. Reuse fsck's orphan predicate so the finding remains repairable. With no readable prior snapshot, exclude nothing.\tPASS\t152\t33\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_rollback_fold\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_rollback_fold\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py#D:_rollback_fold\tRestore retired sources and unstage the ticket directory. Remove the new snapshot only if every source returns. Otherwise keep it for fsck repair so a failed rollback cannot lose folded events.\tPASS\t121\t31\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer.py#D:create_core\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/composer.py#D:create_core\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/composer.py#D:create_core\tValidate and append CREATE, then return id, alias, and title. Validate type, title, priority, initialization, and parent before writing. Optional source fields record import provenance with a fresh local ID and timestamp. Required creation_channel records the validated ingress source.\tPASS\t179\t39\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#D:<module>\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#D:<module>\tEDIT command composition shared by library and CLI. This leaf owns field validation, tag deltas, parent checks, and the CLI parser. composer re-exports its entry points for existing callers.\tPASS\t124\t29\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#D:edit_core\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#D:edit_core\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#D:edit_core\tValidate edits and append EDIT plus any compiled TAG_DELTA. Reject unknown or invalid fields and parent cycles. Tag set becomes an add-wins delta against observed tags. Return an advisory description-cap warning after a successful oversized description edit, otherwise None.\tPASS\t161\t39\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:_rc = _edit_govern(ticket_id):1\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:_rc = _edit_govern(ticket_id):1\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:_rc = _edit_govern(ticket_id):1\t# Keep the custom EDIT grammar here for arbitrary fields, tag deltas, # and exact errors. The factory still governs through _edit_govern.\tPASS\t83\t19\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:from rebar._commands import _confirm:1\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:from rebar._commands import _confirm:1\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:from rebar._commands import _confirm:1\t# Confirm field names only, in invocation order.\tPASS\t14\t7\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:_warn_stderr(edit_warning):1\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:_warn_stderr(edit_warning):1\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:_warn_stderr(edit_warning):1\t# Warn on stderr after saving and before optional review.\tPASS\t36\t9\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:from rebar import llm  # LAZY — preserves optionality:1\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:from rebar import llm  # LAZY — preserves optionality:1\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py#C:edit_cli:before:from rebar import llm  # LAZY — preserves optionality:1\t# Run optional plan review after the EDIT commits and releases its lock. # The edit remains saved whatever the review verdict.\tPASS\t65\t20\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:<module>\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:<module>\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:<module>\tRead-only diagnosis of store and worker locks. Report held legs, stamped owner, same-host liveness, age, and staleness through the shared lock helpers. An active holder is informational. A stale lock is a finding. O_EXCL workers write owner stamps. Older unstamped files use the shared wall-clock rule. Doctor never reclaims locks, including under repair. The snapshot-GC worker lock is read from the per-host snapshot store without creating that store.\tPASS\t634\t68\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:_mkdir_report\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:_mkdir_report\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:_mkdir_report\tReport the tickets-store mkdir lock's owner, age, liveness, and shared staleness verdict. Missing or torn stamps remain unknown until the shared wall-clock rule can decide.\tPASS\t96\t25\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\nsrc/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:_existence_report\tb10a2309d65b4128c30dd7839a6d9905b8158e63:src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:_existence_report\tc1ec32a1996bdda0ed287c44ef8a1c9ea1b57135:src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py#D:_existence_report\tReport an O_EXCL worker lock when its file exists. Read its stamped owner and ask the shared helper for liveness and staleness. Older unstamped files follow the same wall-clock rule. This diagnostic never reclaims the file.\tPASS\t106\t36\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root/resume_group04:2026-10-23\n```"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792814503364636356,"uuid":"54f83500-229d-46c8-b716-0c46228cb72a"}